    "Full API spec": "Public API surface (imported via 'from flappy_bird import Game, Pipe, Config' and 'from flappy_bird.scoring import is_pipe_scored'):\n\n- Module: flappy_bird.config\n  - class Config:\n    - Attributes (floats unless noted): gravity, flap_impulse, max_vy, bird_x, start_y, pipe_speed, pipe_width, gap_height, world_height, world_ceiling, world_floor; spawn_interval_ticks: int.\n    - Semantics: Immutable-like configuration holder used by Game and domain helpers. Validation ensures coherent ranges (e.g., world_ceiling < world_floor, gap_height > 0, pipe_width > 0, max_vy > 0, spawn_interval_ticks >= 1).\n\n- Module: flappy_bird.pipes\n  - class Pipe:\n    - Constructor: Pipe(x: float, gap_y: float, width: float, gap_height: float, passed: bool = false)\n    - Methods:\n      - right_edge() -> float: returns x + width\n      - step(speed: float) -> None: mutates x := x - speed per tick\n    - Attributes: x, gap_y, width, gap_height, passed (bool)\n\n- Module: flappy_bird.physics\n  - clamp(value: float, lo: float, hi: float) -> float: returns value clamped into [lo, hi]\n  - integrate_vy(vy: float, gravity: float, max_vy: float) -> float: returns clamp(vy + gravity, -max_vy, max_vy)\n\n- Module: flappy_bird.scoring\n  - is_pipe_scored(bird_x: float, pipe_right_edge: float, already_passed: bool) -> bool\n    - Pure helper; returns True exactly when (not already_passed) and (pipe_right_edge < bird_x). Implements a strict-left rule: scoring occurs only after the pipe's right edge is strictly left of the bird_x. Idempotent: once already_passed is True, never re-scores.\n\n- Module: flappy_bird.collision\n  - hits_bounds(y: float, ceiling: float, floor: float) -> bool: returns True if y is above ceiling or below floor\n  - hits_pipe(bird_x: float, bird_y: float, pipe: Pipe) -> bool: returns True if the bird overlaps the pipe's solid regions horizontally and is not within the vertical gap centered at pipe.gap_y of height pipe.gap_height\n\n- Module: flappy_bird.game\n  - class Game:\n    - __init__(self, config: Config, initial_pipes: list[Pipe] = []) -> None\n      - Initializes state='ready', tick=0, score=0, bird_y=config.start_y, bird_vy=0.0, internal pipe list from initial_pipes (copied). No I/O.\n    - reset(self) -> None\n      - Resets to the initial 'ready' state and clears score and pipes.\n    - flap(self) -> None\n      - If state == 'game_over': no-op.\n      - If state == 'ready': set state='running' atomically and immediately apply flap impulse: bird_vy := bird_vy + (-abs(config.flap_impulse)) or directly set to the impulse value as defined by design; effect is an immediate upward velocity change before next step().\n      - If state == 'running': reapply the same impulse to bird_vy.\n    - step(self) -> None\n      - If state != 'running': increments tick and returns without altering y/vy/pipes/score.\n      - While 'running', applies deterministic order per tick:\n        1) bird_vy := physics.integrate_vy(bird_vy, config.gravity, config.max_vy)\n        2) bird_y := bird_y + bird_vy\n        3) Move all pipes: for each pipe, pipe.step(config.pipe_speed)\n        4) Scoring: for each pipe with pipe.passed == False, compute right = pipe.right_edge(); if scoring.is_pipe_scored(config.bird_x, right, pipe.passed) then set pipe.passed=True and increment score by 1. 'passed' remains true while the pipe remains listed.\n        5) Collision checks: if collision.hits_bounds(bird_y, config.world_ceiling, config.world_floor) or any collision.hits_pipe(config.bird_x, bird_y, pipe) then set state='game_over'.\n        6) Removal: after scoring, remove any pipes whose right_edge() < 0 (fully off-screen) in the same tick.\n        7) Increment tick by 1 at the end of step.\n    - pipes_readonly(self) -> tuple[Pipe, ...]\n      - Returns an immutable snapshot tuple of current pipes, including those with passed == True until they are removed off-screen.\n    - status(self) -> dict\n      - Returns a plain dict snapshot: {'state': str, 'tick': int, 'y': float, 'vy': float, 'score': int, 'pipes': list[dict]} where each pipe dict includes x, gap_y, width, gap_height, passed.\n\n- Module: flappy_bird.__init__\n  - Re-exports: Game, Pipe, Config\n\nImport direction and acyclicity rules:\n- flappy_bird/config.py has no imports.\n- flappy_bird/physics.py and flappy_bird/scoring.py import only typing; they do not import domain entities.\n- flappy_bird/pipes.py imports only typing.\n- flappy_bird/collision.py imports typing and flappy_bird.pipes for the Pipe type.\n- flappy_bird/game.py imports: config, physics, scoring, collision, pipes.\n- Main.py imports only flappy_bird public API.\n\nError behavior:\n- Public methods do not raise on normal game flow. ValueError may be raised only during Config construction/validation if parameters are invalid.\n- All functions are synchronous and side-effect free except for Game and Pipe methods which mutate instance state.\n\nVersion constraints:\n- Python 3.10 syntax only; avoid 3.11+ features.",
    "Shared Knowledge": "Protocol requires preserving requirements.txt, Main.py, and tests/test_main.py exactly by path. The core reusable logic is under flappy_bird/* with an acyclic graph: config (root), pure rules (physics, scoring), entity (pipes), collision (imports Pipe), orchestration (game) importing the others, and __init__ re-exporting the public API. Tests import only via public paths: from flappy_bird import Game, Pipe; from flappy_bird.scoring import is_pipe_scored; from flappy_bird.config import Config. No GUI or I/O in tests.",
    "Execution Protocol": "Run tests with: python -m pytest -q. Exactly one protocol-level test file exists: tests/test_main.py. The runtime demo entry is Main.py, executed headlessly (python Main.py), but tests do not import or execute Main.py. Additional files must not alter protocol files.",
    "Anything UNCLEAR": "There is a minor tension between 'pure rules (physics, scoring, collision) only depend on typing and config types' and the specified collision signature hits_pipe(bird_x, bird_y, pipe: Pipe), which necessarily imports Pipe. Plan follows the class diagram and call flow by letting collision import Pipe, which remains acyclic."
}
